  "title": "920th Rescue Wing Hurricane Michael Relief",
  "description": "Airmen from the 334th Air Expeditionary Group take off to survey the Florida panhandle, Oct. 11, 2018 from Patrick Air Force Base, Florida, after Hurricane Michael left its mark on the peninsula coast. The 334th AEG is an expeditioary search and rescue unit made up of Reserve Citizen Airmen from the 920th Rescue Wing, PAFB, Florida and the 563rd Rescue Group, Davis-Monthan Air Force Base, Arizona. Aircrew took off in two HH60-G Pave Hawk helicopters and an HC-130P/N King aerial refueling aircraft. The 334th AEG is standing by to perform search and rescue if called upon by Federal Emergency Management Agency.",
